==English==

===Interjection===
{{en-interj|head=[[land]] [[ahoy]]}}

# {{context|nautical|lang=en}} Modern erroneous interjection (the real term is "land ho") shouted by the [[ship]]'s [[watch]] to inform the crew that land has been [[spot]]ted. "Ahoy" is a hailing call and so would never be used in reference to any person (much less on object) from which the caller does not expect a response. The land-bound equivalent is "Hello, there!"
